<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistani interbank rates dive on low borrowing.</title>
<headline>Pakistani interbank rates dive on low borrowing.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1996-12-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's interbank money market rates dived on Monday on low borrowing before the year-end, dealers said.</p>
<p>The market opened at 20 percent and fell to 10 percent in the absence of borrowing pressure, one dealer at the Standard Chartered Bank in Karachi said.</p>
<p>&quot;At the close of the day, however, the rates managed to climb up to 13.00 and 13.50 percent,&quot; the dealer said.</p>
<p>-- Ibrahim Khan 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
